  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    # Remove the outermost border (1 cell layer from each side)\n    if len(grid) <= 2 or len(grid[0]) <= 2:\n        return []\n    \n    # Extract inner grid\n    inner = [row[1:-1] for row in grid[1:-1]]\n    \n    h = len(inner)\n    w = len(inner[0]) if h > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Rotate 90 degrees clockwise\n    # New grid has dimensions w x h\n    rotated = [[inner[h - 1 - j][i] for j in range(h)] for i in range(w)]\n    \n    return rotated\n```",
